1. Core Gameplay Mechanics
1.1 Set up Box2D physics engine integration with Qt
1.2 Implement paddle with keyboard and/or mouse controls
1.3 Develop ball launch mechanism with realistic bounce behavior
1.4 Create collision handling between ball, paddle, bricks, and walls
1.5 Design and render bricks as labeled answer choices
1.6 Configure bricks to respond differently based on answer correctness
1.7 Implement scoring system based on breaking correct vs incorrect bricks
1.8 Enforce a 15-second timer for each round
1.9 Define win/loss conditions based on accuracy and time expiration

2. Trivia System & Educational Content
2.1 Create a structured trivia question database (JSON or SQLite)
2.2 Populate trivia database with topics (capitals, countries, landmarks, flags)
2.3 Design and implement a trivia loader that injects new questions per round
2.4 Assign answers to corresponding bricks at game start

3. Learning Phase
3.1 Design interactive 2D map UI with country outlines and labels
3.2 Display relevant educational data (e.g., capital, flag, landmark) per topic
3.3 Enable player to interact with map before each round
3.4 Add “Start Challenge” button to begin the brick-breaking phase

4. Post-Round Feedback System
4.1 Display correct answers after each round ends
4.2 Highlight any incorrect answers the player hit
4.3 Show brief fun facts related to each missed answer
4.4 Store performance data for later progress tracking

5. User Interface & Experience
5.1 Design and implement main menu (Start Game, View Progress, Quit)
5.2 Build game UI with paddle, ball, brick area, question display, and timer
5.3 Implement pause/resume functionality
5.4 Create smooth transitions between learning, gameplay, and feedback phases
5.5 Style game elements for a visually engaging and clean UI

6. Game Loop & Progress Tracking
6.1 Implement round lifecycle: load → learn → play → review
6.2 Track round-based stats (score, accuracy, correct answers)
6.3 Persist player progress using local storage (file or lightweight DB)
6.4 Build a "View Progress" screen displaying historical performance

7. Asset Integration
7.1 Collect and integrate image assets (flags, maps, brick textures)
7.2 Optimize and scale assets for use in game scenes
7.3 Organize asset loading and resource management code

8. Technical Setup & Collaboration
8.1 Set up initial Qt project with Box2D library and structured file system
8.2 Initialize GitHub repository with README and license
